# Workshop Goal
Create your first dynamically controlled visuals on the LED Matrix. It can done using the animation method, canvas method, or both. This can be simple, but focus on creating a clear relationship between the type of input and output.

# Resources
- Arduino
- Distance Sensor
- 4 Plug/Header jumper wires
- pressure sensor kit (get it from Nick)
- Alligator clip jumper wires
- 220 ohm resistor

# Activity
start from the examples shown from today, but create a simple first interaction for both the distance sensor and the pressure sensor. 
- Start by writing out a simple description of what the interaction is: for example, "When I XXXXXX the screen shows YYYYYY" etc. 
- Write out the simple pseudo code in plain language the steps needed to achieve it
- Create a simple version of the code that does the simplest version of the interaction
- Make it better

Do this for both sensors. The visuals should be different for the different interactions

# Submission
Your post should consist of the following components

- Distance Sensor
- - Your 1 sentence description of the interaction
- - Your pseudo code. This can be written out as text or an image of a drawing/diagram
- - An image that shows your input and sensor

- Pressure Sensor
- - Your 1 sentence description of the interaction
- - Your pseudo code. This can be written out as text or an image of a drawing/diagram
- - An image that shows your input and sensor